    "title": "Enphase Energy Inc (ENPH) Q1 2026 Earnings Call Highlights: Strong Revenue Amidst Market Challenges",
    "byline": null,
    "published_at": null,
    "site_name": "finance.yahoo.com",
    "language": null
  },
  "content": {
    "text": "This article first appeared on GuruFocus.\n-\nRevenue: $282.9 million for Q1 2026.\n-\nGross Margin (Non-GAAP): 43.9% in Q1 2026.\n-\nGross Margin (GAAP): 35.5% in Q1 2026.\n-\nOperating Expenses (Non-GAAP): $77 million for Q1 2026.\n-\nOperating Expenses (GAAP): $130 million for Q1 2026.\n-\nOperating Income (Non-GAAP): $47.3 million for Q1 2026.\n-\nOperating Loss (GAAP): $29.6 million for Q1 2026.\n-\nNet Income (Non-GAAP): $62.3 million for Q1 2026.\n-\nNet Loss (GAAP): $7.4 million for Q1 2026.\n-\nDiluted EPS (Non-GAAP): $0.47 for Q1 2026.\n-\nDiluted Loss Per Share (GAAP): $0.06 for Q1 2026.\n-\nFree Cash Flow: $83 million for Q1 2026.\n-\nCash, Cash Equivalents, and Marketable Securities: $930.6 million as of March 31, 2026.\n-\nMicroinverters Shipped: 1.41 million units in Q1 2026.\n-\nBatteries Shipped: 103 megawatt-hours in Q1 2026.\n-\nSafe Harbor Revenue: $34.5 million in Q1 2026.\n-\nQ2 Revenue Guidance: $280 million to $310 million.\n-\nQ2 Safe Harbor Revenue Guidance: Approximately $85 million.\n-\nQ2 Gross Margin Guidance (GAAP): 42% to 45%.\n-\nQ2 Gross Margin Guidance (Non-GAAP): 44% to 47%.\nRelease Date: April 28, 2026\nFor the complete transcript of the earnings call, please refer to the full earnings call transcript.\nPositive Points\n-\nEnphase Energy Inc (NASDAQ:ENPH) reported a strong quarterly revenue of $282.9 million, with significant shipments of 1.41 million microinverters and 103 megawatt-hours of batteries.\n-\nThe company achieved a record Net Promoter Score (NPS) of 82% in Q1, indicating high customer satisfaction.\n-\nEnphase Energy Inc (NASDAQ:ENPH) is expanding its AI assistant rollout to enhance customer and installer support, improving efficiency and service quality.\n-\nThe company is making significant progress in Europe, with a 36% revenue increase in Q1 compared to Q4, driven by rising power prices and increased battery adoption.\n-\nEnphase Energy Inc (NASDAQ:ENPH) is actively developing new products, including a fifth-generation battery and a bi-directional EV charger, which are expected to drive future growth.\nNegative Points\n-\nEnphase Energy Inc (NASDAQ:ENPH) experienced a 23% sequential decline in US revenue due to lower residential solar and battery demand following the expiration of tax credits.\n-\nThe company ended Q1 with channel inventory above normal levels, indicating potential challenges in demand forecasting and inventory management.\n-\nGross margin decreased from 46.1% in Q4 to 43.9% in Q1 on a non-GAAP basis, impacted by reciprocal tariffs and other factors.\n-\nThe US residential solar market is facing challenges, including unfavorable weather conditions and TPO financing issues, affecting sell-through expectations.\n-\nEnphase Energy Inc (NASDAQ:ENPH) is facing intense competition in Europe, particularly from low-cost inverter and battery providers, necessitating price reductions to remain competitive.",
